Problem Statement :-

You are climbing a staircase with n steps. Each time, you can climb either 1 step or 2 steps.

Return the number of distinct ways to reach the top of the staircase.

LeetCode: Climbing Stairs...
Instead of storing all previous results in an array, we use only two variables: first and second.Approach: Dynamic Programming (Space Optimized)

The number of ways to climb n stairs follows the Fibonacci sequence.

To reach stair n, you can:

Come from stair n - 1 by taking 1 step.

Come from stair n - 2 by taking 2 steps.

Therefore:

ways(n) = ways(n - 1) + ways(n - 2)//







class Solution {
    public int climbStairs(int n) {
        if (n <= 2) {
            return n;
        }

        int first = 1;
        int second = 2;

        for (int i = 3; i <= n; i++) {
            int third = first + second;
            first = second;
            second = third;
        }

        return second;
    }
}
